{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/364096-occultism-in-dtd","id":364096,"title":"Occultism in DtD","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-08T21:58:18-08:00","id":364096,"title":"Occultism in DtD","content":"Okay, in Antagonists there is discussion about occultism, folk magic that muggles can use, the magic might come from an item, from the ritual itself, or an outside force or entity reacting to the ritual.<br /> <br /> While in mage such things might be supernal echoes, it seems to me that it could also be explained ala the god-machine as occult matrices.<br /> <br /> While less impressive than the infrastructure of the God-Machine, it's also only likely to be guarded by human occultists or cultists, much less of a threat and a possible future resource to boot.<br /> <br /> So do you think demons would have an equal facility for orphaned occult matrices as infrastructure?<br /> <br /> Also, it occurred to me that the harvesting of these things would allow a demon to build a more occult identity, it's not like the inhabitants of nwod can see your character sheets: people who can do magic probably seem mostly the same whether they are mages, thaumaturges, or collectors of occult matrices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T13:43:05-08:00","id":364742,"title":"","content":"Didn't gmc point out that most of the occult shenanigans that mortals get up too are just them taking advantage of the same quirks in our reality that the machine uses?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","name":"cmwatford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T22:56:06-08:00","id":365127,"title":"","content":"I think the ultimate answer to your question is 'storyteller discretion'. But I think it would make for a very interesting aspect of the game to allow small occult ritual spaces and the like (perhaps even homes decorated to feng shui) to generate very small amounts of aether. Perhaps a demon's suborned infrastructure was not built by the God-Machine, but it is one of his apartment's Covers organized just perfectly to allow the flow of occult power. I especially think this is appropriate since while Demons likewise don't know all the secrets of Infrastructure, they know more than the average human occultist aware of the God-Machine and perhaps this knowledge would allow them to tweak other occult areas to better resonate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T00:27:41-08:00","id":365189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cmwatford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/364096-occultism-in-dtd?p=364742#post364742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't gmc point out that most of the occult shenanigans that mortals get up too are just them taking advantage of the same quirks in our reality that the machine uses?</div> </div> </div> </div> An occult matrix is an infrastructure like effect not created by the god-machine. It's the equivalent of monkey's writing shakespeare, A and B and the rest of the alphabet combine and someone ends up summoning spirits or raising zombies or whatever despite there not being a god-like machine intelligence behind it. <br /> <br /> Demons can sense, collect, and alter infrastructure despite it being protected by the god-machine's forces, but while the book mentions occult matrices, that's all it does- mention them. <br /> <br /> Even if demons can't sense occult matrices because they aren't actually infrastructure or god-machine related at all, they are still aware of the phenomena.<br /> <br /> So how realistic is it that no demon would collect some occult matrices for some extra tricks up their sleeves? <br /> <br /> So even if my assumption that folk magic occultism from Antagonists can be explained as occult matrices is an assumption one doesn't agree with (one might like the supernal echo explanation from mage better for example), the question of occult matrices place in dtd is still a valid question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T05:51:47-08:00","id":365328,"title":"","content":"Well specifically, it's cause and effect. The infrastructure is the raw materials, the occult matrix is the process, the result (such as an angel) is the goal. God-Machine builds infrastructure, all infrastructure generates some sort of occult matrix which ultimately creates an output (the goal of the infrastructure to begin with). Often infrastructure begets larger infrastructure. (Example: A small piece of infrastructure in a recycling plant creating an angel. The angel is the output but it's also a destroyer. It then goes and kills plant workers in a very specific order, the angel itself is then the infrastructure, their ritual death the occult matrix, and an even more potent angel is the output. Which then goes on to do something on a larger scale.) Note: A mechanical gray area exists with infrastructure. I'm unsure if it's dealt with directly in the book but sometimes angels (or even people) can be infrastructure themselves. Does this mean an angel that is itself infrastructure will always generate essence for itself? I doubt it. It's likely &quot;compatible&quot; infrastructure or the infrastructure which created it. But hey, if you want a monster unstoppable angel, go for it?<br /> <br /> So an occult matrix is &quot;magic&quot;. Infrastructure is intertwined and related directly to an occult matrix - as the occult matrix is the infrastructure in motion - but this doesn't mean that any other form of magic couldn't then also be considered an &quot;occult matrix&quot; as all that really means is magic in motion. So an elaborate Mage spell could also be an occult matrix. It just needs to require resources that go into motion to produce an output of some kind.<br /> <br /> Therefore I'd say it's very reasonable to assume that Demons have an understanding of these basic occult physics and would take advantage of them. How far and how deep that rabbit hole goes would be up to the Storyteller though as arguments could be made then that, say, a Mummy's tomb is a massive piece of infrastructure and generates an occult matrix powered by Sekhem instead of Essence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T10:12:25-08:00","id":365491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DesolateDolly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/364096-occultism-in-dtd?p=365328#post365328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note: A mechanical gray area exists with infrastructure. I'm unsure if it's dealt with directly in the book but sometimes angels (or even people) can be infrastructure themselves. Does this mean an angel that is itself infrastructure will always generate essence for itself? I doubt it. It's likely &quot;compatible&quot; infrastructure or the infrastructure which created it. But hey, if you want a monster unstoppable angel, go for it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Insofar as strict adherence to the Ephemeral Being rules is a thing, the &quot;Infrastructure&quot; that gives a given angel Essence <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/71851-unpacking-manifestation-conditions?p=185555#post185555\">is particular to what it has Influence over</a>; particularly mobile angels tend to have at least a token dot in a more ubiquitous Influence, like Time or Gravity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}